ndows/Android, and be invisible on ios/macos.\nIf you just move the GPUParticles2D to be a child of Root instead, then it works everywhere.\n\nI believe this might be related to #96030 #95797\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a scene, create a CanvasGroup node (default settings) and a GPUParticles2D node (default processing material probably work).\nExport to web, visit the page on a WebKit browser.\nParticles will be invisible (and visible with other browsers)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[ios-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28934223/ios-bug.zip)\n\nNote: I don't actually have an iphone or mac. I was able to borrow one to test the issue extensively on my game, so I'm pretty sure my description is accurate, but I didn't actually test this MRP.\nTell me if the issue doesn't appear here and I'll update it with the actual scene from my game then.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120302/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120302/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}